{% decision_card number="ADR-0009" status="approved" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

An authoring model or session has correlated blind spots and cannot independently approve itself.

## Decision drivers

- Reviewer independence
- Defect discovery
- Evidence-based convergence

## Options considered

- Self-review
- Same provider/session review
- Other provider plus fresh-session panel

## Decision

Use the other eligible provider for critique and exclude the authoring session from approval votes.

## Positive consequences

- Reduces correlated review
- Makes ownership explicit

## Negative consequences

- Adds latency and provider usage

## Risks

- Ritual duplicate review can waste tokens on low-risk work

## Follow-up work

- Scale review to risk
- Track whether second voice finds material defects

## Supersedes or superseded by

New decision; superseded by: none.

